WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.940
Templates can move complex work into compile time.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:12.920
constexpr functions, recursive templates, type computation, generated overload sets, and metaprogramming can improve performance or expressiveness.

3
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:19.500
They can also create build-time cost, code bloat, difficult diagnostics, and hard-to-review behavior.

4
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:25.620
A design that creates many instantiations may increase binary size and make verification harder.

5
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:32.200
A template that expands through many layers can produce compiler errors that few engineers can interpret.

6
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:39.820
A clever metaprogram can hide a security decision from ordinary code review because the decision is encoded in type machinery rather than straightforward control flow.

7
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.260
Resource control is therefore part of defensive template design.

8
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:53.400
Teams should monitor build impact for template-heavy libraries, keep expansion patterns understandable, and avoid generating large families of code unless the value is clear.

9
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.660
Simpler generic designs are often safer because more engineers can review them.

10
00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:01.460
Compile-time diagnostics should guide safe use.

11
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:10.360
If a template rejects a type, the error should point toward the violated contract rather than a maze of internal implementation details.

12
00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:15.580
Clear diagnostics reduce pressure to make constraints looser just to silence compiler noise.

13
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:23.220
Use compile-time computation where it improves the design, but keep reviewability, build cost, and binary impact visible.

14
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.540
Build metrics can be useful governance signals.

15
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:36.800
A sudden increase in compile time, object size, or template depth may indicate that a generic design is becoming harder to maintain and verify.
